c = \sqrt{20^2 + 15^2} = \sqrt{400 + 225} = \sqrt{625} = 25 \text{ inches}
\]

The perimeter of the right triangle is the sum of the lengths of its sides: \[
20 + 15 + 25 = 60 \text{ inches}
\]

The perimeter of the square is equal to the perimeter of the right triangle, so the perimeter of the square is also 60 inches. Since a square has four equal sides, the side length \(s\) of the square is given by: \[
4s = 60 \implies s = \frac{60}{4} = 15 \text{ inches}
\]

The area of the square is the side length squared: \[
\text{Area} = s^2 = 15^2 = 225 \text{ square inches}
\]

